+### [ShardedVolume](12593-shardedvolume.md)
+A data structure that represents a 3D volume partitioned into multiple independent shards (sub-arrays) to facilitate parallel processing and memory management across devices or memory spaces. It solves the problem of managing large volumetric datasets that exceed single-device memory or require distributed computation by treating each shard as an autonomous unit. Unlike [Chunk-based World Streaming](2369-chunk-based-world-streaming.md), which focuses on temporal or spatial streaming of chunks for rendering, ShardedVolume emphasizes arithmetic operations and direct data access patterns over a partitioned layout. It differs from [MPI-based Volume Partitioning](1093-mpi-based-volume-partitioning.md) by providing a high-level API for local shard manipulation and concatenation rather than focusing solely on inter-process communication protocols. Choose this for distributed arithmetic operations and slice extraction across partitioned layouts.
 
 ### [Tide: Trajectory-Adaptive Differential Streaming](10150-tide-trajectory-adaptive-differential-streaming.md)
-Tide is a residency-aware data transfer policy for out-of-core volume rendering and training that reuses resident blocks across iterations, transferring only incoming resident deltas to reduce PCIe volume under smooth camera motion [10150-tide-trajectory-adaptive-differential-streaming.md]. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Chunk-based World Streaming](2369-chunk-based-world-streaming.md) by explicitly maintaining a capacity-bounded resident set and using a scoring function to select which blocks to keep in VRAM, rather than simply streaming all visible blocks or using a fixed eviction policy. Choose this for bandwidth-constrained environments with smooth camera motion.
